# Swamp Stomper

## Lore

Also called the Frontiersman, the Swamp Stomper is a Wilderness Scout who has made Dinosaur Swamp his specialty. He knows its diseases, remedies, dinosaurs, barbarian tribes and trading posts, and above all the quickest and safest ways through the swamps and everglades. Like other scouts he hunts and traps, and he is happier in the wild than in any town.

Part of the job is guiding: adventurers, travellers and settlers hire him to get through the swamp alive, and townsfolk send for him when someone is lost, taken by raiders or a dinosaur, or when a rare herb is needed. The pay is poor because the region is poor, and often comes as goods, metals, artifacts or services rather than credits. Because he also deals with mercenaries and other scouts, he can trade them things local villages have no use for.

Stompers are earthy, independent and tough, uneasy in civilized places but comfortable with modern equipment. Outsiders romanticize the life; the swamp swallows the careless.

## GM Notes

Starting kit beyond what the sheet lists: a suit of light or medium Mega-Damage armor (light is usual for silence and movement; an experienced Stomper may own one of each), two pairs of boots (light and heavy leather) with spare laces, a hat and/or helmet, 1D4 waterproof sacks, a 20 foot spool of wire and a 20 foot ball of string, four wooden and two iron spikes, a folding utility knife, a fish gutting knife, a folding saw and a dozen pencil-sized chemical lights.

Weapons: one for each W.P. plus 1D4 E-Clips each where they apply. Most have one or two favourites handed down by family or a mentor, old but well kept, possibly a minor magic item at the G.M.''s discretion.

Vehicles: a two-seat canoe or kayak and a flat bottom boat worked by paddle and pole. From third level, likely an air-foil everglades fan boat and a motorcycle, jeep or hovercycle as well. Most travel light.

Tracking dinosaurs (+20%) is part of the Track Animals skill for this class; the sheet carries it as the separate Track Dinosaurs grant.
